sections.teaching:
添煩，添亂，添污(Tim Woo)
Kam Woo (*Kaml) 's teaching is boring. But he uses iprs and lab test to force you to listen his lecture.

Totally bad course arrangement.

First, kaml treats his lectures as placement marketing of robotic team. He asked his robotic team's member to sell during lectures and introduce the details of robotic team. Which is extremely annoying as I am not interested in them.

Fox's teaching is good. However, his tone is very cocky, he will blame you if you ask stupid questions. He will neither answer nor help you if he think your problem can be solved by yourself. His grading standard also very strict, a slightly error still cannot be passed. But his age that personality is reasonable, I cannot have reason to blame him.

For the remaining TAs, they are very unreliable, even they got A+ with full mark in this course. Actually they took this course with final exam in COVID. However, they are very unreliable. The "Chinese last name" lab, the TA misread the instruction (at least 24x24). Ended with a question: "Why your name very big".
WTF??? This is totally bullshit, I need to open the lab instruction to him to explain to him.
He had another question, why 草花頭（艹）是+ |- ? WTF? 正體字是這樣寫的？你他媽不會寫中文，都不要在這裡吹毛求疵啊老細。這些人沒文化加上沒腦子，很難相處。。。

They even don't know what pointer in C-programming is... During the last lab, they help me to debug my circuit by checking my code.

Here is the code I wrote
int *px = &x;
int *py = &y;
*px = integer_reading_of_compass;
*py = integer_reading_of_compass;

They changed my code to be like this...
int *px = &x;
int *py = &y;
px = integer_reading_of_compass;
py = integer_reading_of_compass;

This is surprising, they even don't know pointer is. Cannot imagine how low standard they are. At the end, we checked that is their hardware in lab kit have problems, even I have changed one set of equipments. This also proves that the lab kits are kind of problematic.

For the TA guesting lectures. Kaml asked those TAs to share their fyp, or robotic project that they have done before. However, kaml wants us to listen carefully with their yapping. He asked each TA to prepare 5 iprs questions!!! This despotic behaviour is even worse that those secondary school teachers who enforce us to listen talks. 2 guest lectures, 20 iprs in total... Useless in final project and course work. Also completely waste our time.

